{"w":2400,"lines":[{"w":0.060150375366210956,"h":0.014576064488692864,"y":0.072674418683461806,"t":"Test 4","x":0.14285714267403737,"c":1},{"x":0.13876583885033947,"y":0.10838209623265682,"c":1,"w":0.76931477864583331,"h":0.035097889798883508,"t":"unforgeable banknotes. He drew up plans for a \"frigidariun' to keep provisions such as meat,"},{"t":"tish, fruit and vegetables fresh. His celebrated design for a prison to be known as a 'Panopticon',","h":0.031669811978312534,"x":0.1389560723732354,"y":0.12888508228523254,"w":0.79157231648763038,"c":1},{"w":0.77499944051106762,"c":1,"y":0.14717364024546831,"x":0.13877961634462138,"h":0.032558974188063527,"t":"in which prisoners would be kept in solitary continement while being visible at all times to the"},{"x":0.14055567258091298,"y":0.16549380928776292,"w":0.76948888142903638,"h":0.034677582867899348,"t":"guards, was very nearly adopted. (Surprisingly, Davies does not discuss the fact that Bentham","c":1},{"y":0.18385846786395521,"h":0.034043338478417562,"c":1,"w":0.79374562581380204,"x":0.13877078562789508,"t":"meant his Panopticon not just as a model prison but also as an instrument of control that could be"},{"t":"applied to schools and factories.)","x":0.13909774117755944,"w":0.2763157908121745,"h":0.016097875080489432,"y":0.21506761111826123,"c":1},{"y":0.24035261484364501,"t":"Bentham was also a pioneer of the \"science of happinessi, If happiness is to be regarded as","x":0.13880844889189034,"w":0.74865183512369804,"c":1,"h":0.030488735771301956},{"t":"a science, it has to be measured, and Bentham suggested two ways in which this might be","y":0.26029732641650949,"x":0.13876306439548605,"w":0.7411746724446614,"h":0.029132015230727837,"c":1},{"h":0.028950147757742073,"c":1,"x":0.13699926781077398,"w":0.77675623575846342,"y":0.27920068010793808,"t":"done. Viewing happiness as a complex of pleasurable sensations, he suggested that it might be"},{"x":0.1388358477315064,"c":1,"y":0.29887421668603253,"t":"quantitied by measuring the human pulse rate. Alternatively, money could be used as the standard","h":0.027215584277799687,"w":0.79744455973307304},{"t":"for quantification: if two different goods have the same price, it can be claimed that they produce","x":0.13699779624992914,"w":0.79546137491861979,"y":0.31671333626911702,"h":0.027465390452859673,"c":1},{"h":0.024988673075659329,"t":"the same quantity of pleasure in the consumer. Bentham was more attracted by the latter measure.","x":0.13709140280518209,"y":0.33780094068582378,"w":0.80094767252604171,"c":1},{"h":0.029415701714470832,"x":0.1388359778327331,"w":0.78053161621093747,"c":1,"t":"By associating money so closely to inner experience, Davies writes, Bentham 'set the stage for","y":0.35325761107360776},{"c":1,"h":0.026007807646270642,"w":0.78610010782877604,"x":0.13700992029829165,"y":0.37485263957620041,"t":"the entangling of psychological researeh and capitalism that would shape the business practices"},{"y":0.39954925930354268,"w":0.21428571065266924,"c":1,"t":"of the twentieth century*.","h":0.017707662588538287,"x":0.13721804683900521},{"y":0.43151521049028463,"h":0.025682236867340835,"t":"The Happiness Industry describes how the projeet of a science of happiness has become","w":0.73158559163411463,"c":1,"x":0.13889947481763423},{"h":0.023520295879415509,"t":"integral to capitalism. We learn much that is interesting about how economic problems are","x":0.13705254238280473,"w":0.74845687866210941,"c":1,"y":0.45137905043861859},{"x":0.13707526778890744,"t":"being redefined and treated as psychologieal maladies. In addition, Davies shows how the","w":0.74465515136718752,"c":1,"y":0.47082767989204721,"h":0.022766272943402055},{"y":0.48933291531555578,"w":0.7653469340006509,"c":1,"h":0.02320460450319195,"t":"belief that inner states of pleasure and displeasure can be objectively measured has informed","x":0.13707392573565746},{"y":0.50939441479266656,"t":"management studies and advertising. The tendency of thinkers such as J B Watson, the founder","w":0.7840377298990886,"x":0.13712035338986708,"c":1,"h":0.021514644487703904},{"y":0.52755262567937067,"w":0.79538289388020822,"h":0.022957575221408622,"x":0.13709472353125166,"c":1,"t":"of behaviourism*, was that human beings could be shaped, or manipalated, by policymakers and"},{"x":0.1370796526421994,"y":0.54623788147182761,"h":0.022956086678882603,"c":1,"w":0.7935166422526041,"t":"managers. Watson had no factual basis for his view of human action. When he became president"},{"t":"of the American Psychological Association in 1915, he 'had never even studied a single human","y":0.56655579376034504,"w":0.78402659098307304,"h":0.020997208928724143,"x":0.13712723168703131,"c":1},{"x":0.13721803393252419,"y":0.5856406957112642,"t":"being': his research had been contined to experiments on white rats. Yet Watson's reductive","c":1,"w":0.75751881917317709,"h":0.019010467062592129},{"t":"model is now widely applied, with 'behaviour change' becoming the goal of governments: in","y":0.60463618771765526,"x":0.13721804285347161,"w":0.76879699707031246,"h":0.018995492594977459,"c":1},{"t":"Britain, a 'Behaviour Insights Team' has been established by the government to study how people","x":0.13710506482394635,"y":0.62053908673850566,"h":0.025166994820697286,"w":0.80103820800781245,"c":1},{"h":0.021879258803682577,"y":0.64228776687685352,"w":0.76330042521158847,"t":"can be encouraged, at minimum cost to the public purse, to live in what are considered to be","x":0.13714976850385635,"c":1},{"y":0.66419832587861383,"t":"socially desirable ways.","x":0.13721804713915389,"w":0.20112781524658205,"h":0.016097875080489321,"c":1},{"x":0.13721803617850337,"c":1,"t":"Modern industrial societies appear to need the possibility of ever-increasing happiness to","y":0.70057952348531327,"w":0.73872182210286463,"h":0.017443732453866434},{"y":0.71652575951270403,"h":0.024114451558837069,"x":0.13713321722429062,"c":1,"t":"motivate them in their labours. But whatever its intellectual pedigree, the idea that governments","w":0.78780670166015621},{"y":0.73824855122509525,"x":0.137218050496483,"w":0.70300750732421879,"h":0.017707662588538287,"c":1,"t":"should be responsible for promoting happiness is always a threat to human freedom."},{"y":0.95423223851162142,"w":0.51338785807291676,"c":1,"t":"* 'behaviourism': a branch of psychology which is concerned with observable behaviour","h":0.016178912219890762,"x":0.17654891386499399}],"h":3106}